WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.633
To start with these

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.402
new tensions with China.

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:04.471
And this near collision between U.S.

00:00:04.471 --> 00:00:06.272
and Chinese warships.

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.807
That is quite the provocation.

00:00:07.807 --> 00:00:10.110
What's your reaction to that?

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:13.680
Well, I think this is part of a concerted

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:14.981
Chinese effort

00:00:14.981 --> 00:00:16.483
to try and intimidate us

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.985
and obviously the government of Taiwan.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:19.753
These incidents

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:20.587
as your reporter

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:22.222
indicated, both

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.290
on the sea and in the air,

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:27.027
are part of a larger Chinese project.

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:28.728
I think they're trying to warn

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.296
the United States

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.831
about keeping its commitments

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.767
to Taiwan, supplying it with weapons

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:34.467
and the like.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:38.004
We saw a similar speech by the Chinese

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:38.838
defense minister

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.874
at the Shangri-La Conference

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.509
this past weekend.

00:00:42.509 --> 00:00:44.177
And so I think what this requires

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:46.413
is the kind of strategic response

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.348
that shows that the United States,

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.916
whether it's in the Taiwan Strait

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:51.384
or the South China Sea

00:00:51.384 --> 00:00:51.918
or anywhere

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:54.354
else, is simply not going to give up

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:55.622
its rights

00:00:55.622 --> 00:00:57.090
to transit the straits

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.325
to have innocent passage

00:01:00.026 --> 00:01:01.628
for its naval vessels

00:01:01.628 --> 00:01:02.762
and to show to China

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.531
their assertion of sovereignty over

00:01:04.531 --> 00:01:05.865
any part

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.067
of China of the world

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.069
that we don't recognize already is China.

00:01:09.202 --> 00:01:10.170
Something we're simply

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.404
not going to accept?

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:14.307
And let me ask you about North Korea.

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.375
I'm sure you saw this.

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:16.943
Former President Donald Trump recently

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:17.911
praised that country's

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.280
dictator Kim Jong un over the North

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.248
Korea's appointment

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.550
to the board of the World

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:25.251
Health Organization.

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:27.153
What is going on with Trump and Kim

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:27.720
Jong un?

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.022
Why does he keep making

00:01:29.022 --> 00:01:29.989
these kinds of comments

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:32.759
about the North Korean dictator

00:01:33.927 --> 00:01:35.795
Well, your guess is as good as mine

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:36.663
I have.

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.131
In the spirit of our times

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.599
tweeted about this and said,

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.233
this is

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.601
one more piece of evidence

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.502
why Donald Trump

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.170
is not fit to be president.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:46.272
This is no joking matter.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:48.842
Kim Jong un is is a cruel dictator.

00:01:48.842 --> 00:01:49.909
His people are among

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.778
the most impoverished in the world.

00:01:51.778 --> 00:01:53.012
He's building

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:54.481
nuclear weapons and ballistic

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.049
missiles intended to be able to hit

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:57.250
the United States

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.586
and intimidate his regional neighbors.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.455
This is not somebody you pal around with.

00:02:02.455 --> 00:02:02.989
It just shows

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:05.825
Trump has no real understanding

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.727
of the depth of the threat

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.496
that Kim Jong un poses.

00:02:09.496 --> 00:02:09.762
And it's

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.764
why four more years of Trump

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:13.299
in control of foreign policy

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:13.933
would be

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.702
extraordinarily dangerous

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.570
for the United States.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:18.471
And I want to get to that.

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.372
But I remember

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:20.640
covering Trump's summit with Kim

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.343
Jong un and Singapore you were there.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:26.412
Did you see any early warning signs

00:02:26.412 --> 00:02:28.781
of this kind of strange friendship

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:29.816
that they seem to have

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:34.187
Well, we saw a warning signs

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:36.890
in Trump's reaction to these letters that

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:39.526
Kim said to him

00:02:39.526 --> 00:02:41.094
before the Singapore summit.

00:02:41.094 --> 00:02:41.861
And then after.

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:42.395
Now,

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:43.830
there's no doubt in my mind

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.864
these letters were written

00:02:44.864 --> 00:02:46.699
by some Communist Party

00:02:46.699 --> 00:02:48.201
hack and the polit

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:50.203
agitprop bureau of the North

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.071
Korean Worker's Party.

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.573
But they were filled with phrases

00:02:53.573 --> 00:02:54.741
like Your Excellency

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:55.575
and things like that.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:55.808
Trump

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.243
just thought they were love letters.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.345
I mean, I just I shook my head.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:01.080
There wasn't much more I could do

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:02.949
I just don't think he understands

00:03:02.949 --> 00:03:03.883
what he's up against

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.018
when he faces

00:03:05.018 --> 00:03:07.921
the hard men of contemporary

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.355
international affairs.

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:11.691
Kim Jong UN, Vladimir Putin, Xi Jinping

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:15.094
just doesn't know what room is in.

00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:16.129
And this weekend.

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.730
Let's switch to Ukraine,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.165
President Volodymyr Zelensky

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:19.933
told the Wall Street

00:03:19.933 --> 00:03:21.568
Journal Ukraine is ready to launch

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:22.635
its much anticipated

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:23.903
counteroffensive in the war

00:03:23.903 --> 00:03:25.171
against Russia.

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:26.606
In your view, how should the U.S.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.641
assist Ukraine in this counteroffensive

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:31.511
and how much support should they get

00:03:34.314 --> 00:03:36.716
Well, I think we've done a lot.

00:03:36.716 --> 00:03:39.385
From my perspective, we haven't

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:40.019
done enough,

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.754
but I think there's more that we can help

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:42.956
as the battle goes on.

00:03:42.956 --> 00:03:44.524
I do think one important point

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:45.091
to make here

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:48.661
is not to overhype the potential outcome.

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:49.929
Certainly, there's

00:03:49.929 --> 00:03:51.197
nothing in the performance

00:03:51.197 --> 00:03:53.299
of Russian combat arms over the past

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.767
almost 16 months

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:55.935
to give any evidence

00:03:55.935 --> 00:03:58.104
that they'll do a good job in

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.540
defending against the Ukrainian attack.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.375
And certainly we've put a lot of effort

00:04:02.375 --> 00:04:04.110
into training the Ukrainians.

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.112
But it's a very dangerous period

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:07.981
because if the Ukrainians do

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:08.715
well, there will be

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:09.148
some in

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:09.916
Europe will say,

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:12.485
okay, time to stop all this and negotiate

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.354
And if the Ukrainians don't do well,

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:16.189
some of those same people will say,

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:17.857
look, this has gone on long enough.

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.026
So I think managing expectations

00:04:20.026 --> 00:04:21.961
here is important. I understand why.

00:04:21.961 --> 00:04:22.595
So Lansky

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:24.097
wants to increase

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:25.431
the morale of his

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:26.232
of his fighters,

00:04:26.232 --> 00:04:26.566
and that's

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:28.301
obviously the right thing to do.

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:29.902
But I don't think we ought to conclude

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:31.771
we're within weeks of this war ending.

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:32.972
I think that's a very,

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.275
very unlikely outcome of this offensive.

00:04:35.975 --> 00:04:37.844
And let me get to some campaign politics

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:38.878
as it relates to Ukraine.

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.246
I'm just wondering what you thought

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:40.947
of these comments

00:04:40.947 --> 00:04:43.416
from Florida Governor Ron DeSantis.

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.285
That came in response to a question there

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.319
from then

00:04:46.319 --> 00:04:48.554
Fox host Tucker Carlson last March.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.056
DeSantis said While the U.S.

00:04:50.056 --> 00:04:51.491
has many vital national interests

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:52.392
securing our borders

00:04:52.392 --> 00:04:53.893
addressing the crisis of readiness

00:04:53.893 --> 00:04:55.194
within our military,

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.963
achieving energy and security

00:04:56.963 --> 00:04:58.765
and independence, and checking

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.233
the economic, cultural

00:05:00.233 --> 00:05:01.401
and military power

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:02.902
of the Chinese communist party,

00:05:02.902 --> 00:05:04.437
becoming further entangled

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.805
in a territorial dispute

00:05:05.805 --> 00:05:06.572
between Ukraine

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:09.242
and Russia is not one of them.

00:05:09.242 --> 00:05:09.976
There's been some talk

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:10.910
about how he's backed away

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:11.944
from those comments

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:12.578
Ambassador,

00:05:12.578 --> 00:05:14.714
but does the next Republican presidential

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:17.216
nominee need to be a steadfast supporter

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:19.852
of Ukraine in its fight for its survival?

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.421
What did you make of those comments?

00:05:21.421 --> 00:05:22.088
From DeSantis

00:05:24.824 --> 00:05:25.725
Well, I said

00:05:25.725 --> 00:05:25.925
at the

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.360
time I was disappointed,

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.227
but I do believe

00:05:28.227 --> 00:05:29.729
in the prospect of redemption.

00:05:29.729 --> 00:05:31.331
So I think there's still hope.

00:05:31.331 --> 00:05:33.499
Look, this is not a territorial dispute.

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:35.668
This was an unprovoked act of aggression.

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:38.071
It's been bedrock American policy

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:40.673
since 1945 that peace and stability

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:41.908
on the continent of Europe

00:05:41.908 --> 00:05:43.910
are in America's vital interests.

00:05:43.943 --> 00:05:44.844
That's that's why

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:45.745
we formed Naito

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:46.913
and did many other things.

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:49.415
This attack on Ukraine represented

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:50.750
obviously an assault

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.185
on that country

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:54.153
bordered by many NATO's countries

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:55.121
allies treaty

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:56.589
allies of the United States.

00:05:56.589 --> 00:05:58.491
That's one strategic interest.

00:05:58.491 --> 00:06:01.561
Second, the Russian rationale here

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:02.662
is basically

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:04.597
that the terms on which the Soviet

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:07.600
Union broke up, they no longer accept,

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.535
which means that every other former

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.371
Republic of the Soviet Union

00:06:11.371 --> 00:06:13.973
is in danger of the same treatment

00:06:13.973 --> 00:06:15.341
as Ukraine received.

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:17.477
Like Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania,

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:19.278
also NATO's allies.

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:19.979
And finally,

00:06:19.979 --> 00:06:20.913
just very quickly,

00:06:20.913 --> 00:06:23.483
the Chinese are watching this conflict

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:24.550
more than anybody else.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.386
This is not isolated.

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.187
We just talked about

00:06:28.187 --> 00:06:30.857
Chinese provocations near Taiwan.

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:33.192
If the United States and the West

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.962
don't defend Ukraine here,

00:06:36.195 --> 00:06:38.598
I think the Chinese leadership in Beijing

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:40.967
could well conclude there's no way

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:43.102
will come to Taiwan.

00:06:43.102 --> 00:06:44.003
Assistance.

00:06:44.003 --> 00:06:45.872
So so there are important

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:48.908
American interests worldwide at stake

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:50.376
in how we handle Ukraine.

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:50.910
And I hope

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:52.645
the Republican nominee for president

00:06:52.645 --> 00:06:53.446
will be able to make

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:55.181
that point convincingly.

00:06:55.181 --> 00:06:56.582
And before too long,

00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.418
we're going to be getting to debates

00:06:58.418 --> 00:07:01.320
in the Republican Party primary process.

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.389
The RNC has apparently adopted rules

00:07:03.389 --> 00:07:05.158
that say in order to participate

00:07:05.158 --> 00:07:05.892
in the upcoming

00:07:05.892 --> 00:07:07.193
presidential debates,

00:07:07.193 --> 00:07:08.027
you have to pledge

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:10.129
to support the eventual nominee.

00:07:10.129 --> 00:07:11.164
If that's Trump

00:07:12.331 --> 00:07:13.299
would you do that

00:07:13.299 --> 00:07:14.534
if you were one of these candidates?

00:07:14.534 --> 00:07:16.869
I know, I know you've talked about that.

00:07:16.869 --> 00:07:18.404
You'll be a candidate.

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:19.505
Do you plan on participating

00:07:19.505 --> 00:07:20.239
in these debates?

00:07:20.239 --> 00:07:22.308
And would you sign that pledge?

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:24.510
Would you sign on to that pledge?

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.378
Well, I'm

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:27.213
yeah, I'm still thinking about it.

00:07:27.213 --> 00:07:28.815
And no, I wouldn't sign that pledge.

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:31.017
I'm not going to support Donald Trump.

00:07:31.017 --> 00:07:32.952
This is not a matter of party loyalty.

00:07:32.952 --> 00:07:34.020
I think he did

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.289
enormous damage to the country

00:07:36.289 --> 00:07:38.057
and certainly to the Republican Party

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:39.525
in the four years

00:07:39.525 --> 00:07:41.594
he served a second term.

00:07:41.594 --> 00:07:41.994
I think

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:43.596
but all of that is repairable

00:07:43.596 --> 00:07:45.264
and I think it is being repaired.

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:47.133
But four more years of Donald Trump

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:48.000
could do

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.802
significant permanent damage

00:07:49.802 --> 00:07:51.771
to the country and the Republican Party.

00:07:51.771 --> 00:07:52.772
That's so I think

00:07:52.772 --> 00:07:54.173
everybody who's in this race

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:56.542
now should not spend their time

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:58.110
picking away at each other.

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.111
They've got to convince

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:00.780
Republican primary voters

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.850
that the job one here is to prevent

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.285
Trump from big Re-nominated.

00:08:06.886 --> 00:08:07.620
And yesterday,

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.722
we had former Arkansas Governor

00:08:09.722 --> 00:08:11.390
Asa Hutchinson on the program

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.892
and he said that he would,

00:08:12.892 --> 00:08:14.260
as a part of that condition,

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.862
to participate in the debates.

00:08:15.862 --> 00:08:17.463
Yes, he would support Trump

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:19.432
as the eventual nominee.

00:08:19.432 --> 00:08:20.666
Do you think that's a mistake?

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:21.601
And do you think it's a mistake

00:08:21.601 --> 00:08:23.469
for these other candidates in the field

00:08:23.469 --> 00:08:25.238
to sign on to that pledge?

00:08:25.238 --> 00:08:26.205
Should they resist that?

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.774
Well, I

00:08:28.774 --> 00:08:29.242
have a lot

00:08:29.242 --> 00:08:31.043
of respect for as everybody's

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:32.445
got to make up their own mind.

00:08:32.445 --> 00:08:34.747
I didn't vote for Trump in 20, 20.

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:36.449
I didn't vote for Joe Biden either.

00:08:36.449 --> 00:08:37.283
I live in Maryland.

00:08:37.283 --> 00:08:38.150
I wrote in the name

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.086
of a conservative Republican

00:08:40.086 --> 00:08:40.920
because there weren't

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.488
any conservative Republicans on

00:08:42.488 --> 00:08:43.656
the 2020 ballot.

